{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_02_react_readme_render_pipeline", "label": "Render, reconcile, commit", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_02_react_readme_keys_identity", "label": "Keys as identity claims", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Index keys attach state to position rather than item, which is fine for static lists and a bug for reorderable ones; deliberately changing a key is the cleanest way to reset state."}, {"id": "docs_02_react_readme_useeffect_not_lifecycle", "label": "useEffect as synchronisation, not lifecycle", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If a value can be computed during render, an effect is the wrong tool; the three anti-patterns are deriving state in an effect, fetching without cancellation, and resetting state on prop change instead of using a key."}, {"id": "docs_02_react_readme_usesyncexternalstore", "label": "useSyncExternalStore and tearing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Concurrent rendering makes tearing possible with external stores; the selector must be stable or getSnapshot changes identity every render and loops forever, which is why Redux ships a with-selector variant."}, {"id": "docs_02_react_readme_memoisation_policy", "label": "When to memoise", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "useMemo/useCallback are hints React may discard; memoise only for genuinely expensive computation or where identity feeds another hook or a memo'd child. The React Compiler makes manual memoisation largely legacy for pure components."}, {"id": "docs_02_react_readme_perf_checklist", "label": "Ordered React performance checklist", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stated in order (measure, fix state location, cut work, cut re-renders, cut bundle, concurrent features) because saying it in order shows optimisation by measurement rather than reflex. Targets: INP < 200 ms, LCP < 2.5 s, CLS < 0.1."}, {"id": "docs_02_react_readme_testing_house_style", "label": "Testing house style (role queries, userEvent)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Query by role and accessible name so tests exercise the accessibility tree too; test behaviour not implementation. Fake timers with userEvent need advanceTimers, the answer to 'my test hangs'."}, {"id": "docs_02_react_readme_three_kinds_of_state", "label": "Three kinds of state (server, URL, client)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Server state to a query cache, URL state to the URL, client state local until genuinely shared \u2014 naming the three kinds is the senior answer to 'what state management would you pick?'."}, {"id": "docs_02_react_readme_context_performance", "label": "Context has no selector", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every consumer re-renders when the value changes and there is no selector, so split contexts by update frequency or use an external store \u2014 precisely why Zustand and Jotai exist."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_02_react_readme_render_pipeline", "target": "docs_02_react_readme_keys_identity", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_02_react_readme_render_pipeline", "target": "docs_02_react_readme_usesyncexternalstore", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_02_react_readme_useeffect_not_lifecycle", "target": "docs_02_react_readme_keys_identity", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_02_react_readme_useeffect_not_lifecycle", "target": "docs_06_live_coding_readme_race_condition", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_02_react_readme_memoisation_policy", "target": "readme_demo_product_table", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_02_react_readme_perf_checklist", "target": "readme_demo_virtual_list", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_02_react_readme_perf_checklist", "target": "docs_02_react_readme_memoisation_policy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_02_react_readme_usesyncexternalstore", "target": "readme_demo_store_undo_redo", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_02_react_readme_context_performance", "target": "docs_02_react_readme_usesyncexternalstore", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_02_react_readme_testing_house_style", "target": "readme_demo_product_table", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_02_react_readme_three_kinds_of_state", "target": "docs_05_system_design_readme_framework", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_02_react_readme_context_performance", "target": "docs_03_angular_react_vs_angular_hierarchical_di", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/02-react/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}